### (b.1) Codomain re-derived from the effective text's own definitions

R11-5 (as amended by R12-2): e(μ_i) = ramification index of μ_i over the BASE valuation,
cumulative, e(μ_1)=e_1, e(μ_{i+1})=e_{i+1}e(μ_i); Λ_i = (1/e(μ_i))ℤ.
R12-1: dv_i = e(μ_i)·v, v = the base-normalized TERMINAL valuation ν = μ_r.

Then v = μ_r has value group (1/e(μ_r))ℤ = Λ_r by the very definition of e(μ_r), so
  dv_i = e(μ_i)·v  takes values in  e(μ_i)Λ_r = (e(μ_i)/e(μ_r))ℤ.
Since e(μ_r) = e(μ_i)·∏_{j=i+1}^{r} e_j, the index e(μ_i)/e(μ_r) = 1/∏ e_j ≤ 1, so the
group CONTAINS ℤ, with equality iff ∏ e_j = 1 iff e(μ_r)=e(μ_i) — exactly r13's box and
its equality clause. DERIVATION CONFIRMED, independently.
(Λ_i was introduced as the GRADE group and is reused here as v's VALUE group; the two are
the same subgroup of ℚ and r13 writes the formula out, so no conflation error.)

Note the r13 box implicitly excludes 0 (dv_i(0)=+∞ is class (iii)); this is the standard
Γ∪{∞} convention and is not counted.

