(d) VIRGIN SURFACE — honesty ledger vs the unscored §4.2 checks 7-10
================================================================================

Question: does any effective ledger item PRICE a claim on an unscored battery check being
green — i.e. assert as fact something only checks 7, 8, 9 or 10 would establish?

I read all 22 items in effective form. Three touch the unscored teeth:

 * item 18 (r8, gates check 7): "Exact height and normalized residue do not determine an
   admissible corrected-key representative. Every coefficient used in (C3-key) must also
   satisfy \(\deg\widehat k_t<\deg\Phi_i\). Higher-degree, higher-value perturbations are
   excluded by the coefficient-space contract."
   NOT check-dependent: the exclusion is a consequence of the contract's own definition
   (C3-lift-coefficient-space, R8-1 line 3230-3249, \(\mathcal C_i=\{A:\deg A<\deg\Phi_i\}\)).
   Check 7 instruments it; it does not establish it.

 * item 19 (r12, gates check 8): "The displayed residual-read axioms do not imply that the
   base ladder read is a nonzero \(K_i\)-scalar."
   NOT check-dependent. The witness is exhibited in prose (R8-2 line 3328: "Those
   obligations alone permit a read that vanishes on every positive-grade homogeneous
   component") and is elementary — the read R_β := 0 for β>0, := res for β=0 satisfies
   ladder multiplicativity (0 = 0^s for s≥1), graded scalar covariance (0 = 0·res g), the
   grade-zero rule and R(0)=0. I verified this myself; no battery needed.

 * item 22 (r11, names check 9 explicitly): "The canonical residual read is scalar-valued
   only by the site obligation (C3-read-codomain); no displayed read axiom forces it — the
   initial-form read into \(\operatorname{gr}(\mu_i)\) is the standing counterexample
   (§4.2 check 9)."
   The parenthetical CITES an unscored check. But the item's content is the independence
   claim, and the counterexample's validity is argued in R11-1 (line 3657) and is again
   elementary: in(·) is multiplicative on gr(μ_i) (a domain), in(g)≠0 for g≠0 by
   definition, and the grade-0 part is the residue field. The citation locates where the
   claim will be MECHANIZED, not where it is established. I verified the counterexample
   independently. NOT check-dependent.

R11-1's stronger assertion "In particular this mock read PASSES §4.2 check 8" (line 3657)
is likewise a mathematical claim about an unscored check's outcome — but it is argued
(in(N)≠0) and I confirm it. Not a finding.

CONCLUSION for (d): **no ledger item prices on an unscored check being green.** The
