Check 10 (R13-8(iii)) ends:

  > Then score every \(dv\)-site of the effective text against the four consumed classes
  > named in the grade-data paragraph, and fail on any site that consumes a \(dv_i\)-value
  > outside \(\mathbb Z\) or that applies \(dv_i\) to \(\Phi_i^{k}\) with \(e_{i+1}\nmid k\).

The second disjunct says "APPLIES", not "consumes", and the effective text contains three
sites that apply dv_i to Φ_i^k with e_{i+1}∤k — all of them r13's own:
  (1) the grade-data paragraph's witness display,
      > dv_2(\Phi_2) = e(\mu_2)\,\nu(\Phi_2) = 4\cdot\tfrac{21}{8} = \tfrac{21}{2} = \kappa_3 \notin\mathbb Z
  (2) its prose, "In particular (C1-stage-key-height) gives \(dv_i(\Phi_i)=u_{i+1}/e_{i+1}\),
      which is non-integral exactly when \(e_{i+1}\nmid u_{i+1}\)."
  (3) check 10's own instruction, "confirm that \(dv_i(\Phi_i)=u_{i+1}/e_{i+1}\notin\mathbb Z\)".
A mechanical scorer therefore fails the note on the tooth's own specification. This is
precisely the family R4-3 fixed for check 6 ("Make the weld-scope lint exclude its own
specification" — "Occurrences inside this lint specification, quotations of rejected
language, and explicit scope-fence negations are nonmatches"); check 10 carries no such
self-exclusion.

Secondary, same defect: check 10 directs the scorer to score "every dv-site ... against
the four consumed classes", but two dv-sites of the effective text fall in no single
class — the product site (C3-common-height),
